# The control for h5: what a PLAIN start of the same image shows for each brand, so that the
# restored container's answer means something. brand-b's display name is "Inkline"
# (server/src/main/resources/themes/brand-b.json).
plain start with BRAND=brand-a -> "id":"home-brand","text":"Konekt"
plain start with BRAND=brand-b -> "id":"home-brand","text":"Inkline"

# h5-environment.log: the RESTORED container, started with -e BRAND=brand-b, answered
#   {"type":"column","id":"home","children":[{"type":"text","id":"home-brand","text":"Konekt",...
# i.e. brand-a — the value the checkpoint was taken with. The environment of the restore container
# does not reach configuration that was read at startup.
